So, about the story: It's called "The Minister's Black Veil" and was written by this guy called Hawthorne. but more about him later.

In the story. there's a pastor called Mr. Hooper who one day puts on a weird black veNil and it freaks EVERYONE out. What's more is no matter how much people ask, he refuses to take it off. He even refuses to take it off for his wife and that makes her leave him.

The thing I found REALLY COOL about the story though, is how it connects having a face to our humanity. Isn't that INTERESTING?

So basically, the Veil represents a sort of disconnect between Mr. Hooper and everyone else. It told others that he had something to hide.

"But that piece of crape, to their imagination, seemed to hang down before his heart, the symbol of a fearful secret between him and them"

If you take your time to analyze this quote, you'll notice two main things:

1.)
    To the people around Mr. Hooper, he SEEMS like he has a big secret that he's desperate to hide. Of course, the only evidence they have to this is, well, the black veil, which isn't much. Because of this, one can deduce that the people around Mr. Hooper are experiencing an irrational fear of him due to his lack of a face.

    But one thing to not before you judge these Puritans for making assumptions: Remember Slenderman? You know, the retro horror story spread around by the internet, starting about 17 years ago? Yeah, you know the one! Well, if you do, you'll remember what made the character so different from any run-of-the-mill lanky tall guys who scare little kids: He had no face.

    An otherwise normal looking person who has no face is just scary. Like seriously, imagine if you were at McDonalds, or god-forbid Burger King, and the guy taking your order had no face. You wouldn't like that, probably. And yes, the black veil only HIDES Mr. Hooper's face, but the same underlying effect is in place here: It freaks our monkey, no, uh chimpanzee brains out a ton when we can't see someone's face.

2.)
    The Veil is something BETWEEN Mr. Hooper and the others. It is a dividing wall of secrecy between Mr. Hooper and everyone else.
